The paper’s central search problem is indeed native graph structure: find a spanning Halin subgraph, represented by a homeomorphically irreducible spanning tree plus the induced leaf cycle. The main theorem guarantees existence only for sufficiently large graphs with minimum degree at least \((n+1)/2\); I’m now checking the full proof and cited complexity boundary to avoid confusing existential density with average-case hardness.
