   121	
   122	## Caveats
   123	
   124	- The GF(2) affine hiding layer is a structure-preserving vertex relabelling added by the benchmark; it is not a construction used in the paper. The underlying handed object and every checked edge are still the paper's native `Q` graph, so this is not a surrogate reduction.
   125	- The generator covers Proposition 1's two-`H_1` composition, not arbitrary graphs satisfying the paper's asymptotic Dirac condition. Removing the affine promise changes the recovery problem substantially.

