Let $W_1=U_1\cap W$ and $W_2=U_2\cap W$.
By (v) of Claim~\ref{subgraph_K}, we know
that
 there are $|W_1|$ vertex-disjoint 3-stars with centers in $W_1$
and all other vertices in  $U_2-W_2-\{x_1', y_1', x_2', y_2'\}$,
and $|W_2|$ vertex-disjoint 3-stars with centers in $W_2$
and all other vertices in  $U_1-W_1-\{x_1', y_1', x_2', y_2'\}$,
and all these $|W_1|+|W_2|$ stars are vertex-disjoint.
Let $S$ be the union of the 3-stars with centers in $W_2$.

For any $u,v\in U_2-W_2$, $\Gamma(u,v, U_1-W_1-V(S)-\{x'_1, x_2', y_1', y_2'\})\ge 3|W_1|$,
and for any $u,v, w\in U_1-W_1-V(S)$, $\Gamma(u,v, w, U_2-V(S)-\{x'_1, x_2', y_1', y_2'\})\ge 4|W_1|$.
By Lemma~\ref{absorbing2}, we can
find a ladder $L_1$ disjoint from the 3-stars in $S$ with centers in $W_2$
such that $L_1$ is
spanning on $W_1$,
$4|W_1|-1$ vertices from  $U_2-W_2-\{x'_1, x_2', y_1', y_2'\}$,
and another $3|W_1|-1$ vertices from  $U_1-W_1-\{x'_1, x_2', y_1', y_2'\}$,
 if $W_1\ne \emptyset$.

For any $u,v\in U_1-W_1$, $\Gamma(u,v, U_2-W_2-V(L_1)-\{x'_1, x_2', y_1', y_2'\})\ge 3|W_2|$,
and for any $u,v, w\in U_2-W_2$, $\Gamma(u,v, w, U_1-W_1-V(L_1)-\{x'_1, x_2', y_1', y_2'\})\ge 4|W_2|$.
By Lemma~\ref{absorbing2}, we can
find a ladder $L_2$ disjoint from $L_1$
such that $L_2$ is
spanning on $W_2$,
$4|W_2|-1$ vertices from  $U_1-V(L_1)-\{x'_1, x_2', y_1', y_2'\}$,
and another $3|W_2|-1$ vertices from  $U_2-V(L_1)-\{x'_1, x_2', y_1', y_2'\}$,
 if $W_2\ne \emptyset$.

