We have the claim below.


\begin{CLA}\label{spanning ladder}
The balanced bipartite graph
$G''$ contains three vertex-disjoint ladders $Q_1$, $Q_2$, and $ Q_3$
spanning on $V(G'')$
such that the first rung of $Q_1$ is $x_1'x_2'$ and the last rung of $Q_1$
is $a_{11}'a_{21}'$, the first rung of $Q_2$ is $b_{11}'b_{21}'$ and the last rung of $Q_2$
is $a_{12}'a_{22}'$, the first rung of $Q_3$ is $b_{12}'b_{22}'$ and
the last rung of $Q_3$ is $y_1'y_2'$.
