codex
The structure-aware candidate prior is now stricter: at shipping size it conditions on the easily recoverable cap/bridge signature and guesses only the affine map, reducing the claimed search language from roughly 66 bits to 55 bits. That is the honest G4 denominator, and it is still overwhelmingly resistant to random guessing. I’m running the complete measured self-test now, including exact demo enumeration and both reference solvers.
