codex
Built and locally verified, but not yet shippable because the required oracle runs are externally blocked.

The Track B generator uses the paper’s Section 2, Proposition 1 `Q`-composition and affine relabelling ([paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.06181)).

Files:

- [gen_1505_06181.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.06181/gen_1505_06181.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.06181/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.06181/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.06181/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.06181/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.06181/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results include:

- G1: 12/12 planted certificates verified.
- G4: 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses.
- G6: four attacks each succeeded 0/8 times.
- Reference algorithm: 1,252,040 operations, 1.754 seconds average.
- Compact route: 187 operations, 0.083 seconds average.
- G8: 40/40 relabelling checks and 20/20 distinct unrelated instances.
- G9(c): 73 characters, 11 atoms, 37 tokens, 187 operations.

All three hardening runs received HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` before any valid oracle attempt. Those errors are preserved and were not counted as model failures. Restore the OpenRouter key’s total limit, then rerun:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1505_06181.py
```

The family is not rejected; only the required external hardness evidence remains incomplete.
